11734	{"artifactId":"LLD-c32aa60534232f36-s1","entry":{"id":"review-f16ab4a41c4eb63d3b89e3cf6b22a9e7","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-28T11:47:26.066Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's acceptance coverage for s1 (packet provenance/attribution, planless route without index, freshness/staleness detection) matches DEF acceptance criteria s1/ac1-ac4 exactly, and no non-goal (s2-s6 scope) is built here.","evidence":"docs/epics/.../DEF.md:102-105 states ac1 (packets with provenance/parent/merge/line ranges), ac2 (scoped commits, no HEAD/working-tree fallback, ambiguous attribution reported), ac3 (planless/offline route, no invented tasks), ac4 (staleness detection on changed artifacts). LLD §2.1-§2.2, §3.1-§3.2 and §5 cover exactly these four, and §1 'Adjacent scope' explicitly excludes s2-s6 work (evidence ledger, investigation, recovery, completion, composition/MCP). [files: docs/epics/review-planned-changes-through-agent-investigation-E20261028c32aa605/DEF.md, docs/epics/review-planned-changes-through-agent-investigation-E20261028c32aa605/S001/LLD.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's claim that legacy `storyRangeDiff` nets a base..HEAD diff for paths not shared with a merge ('plain' paths), rather than being an immutable-packet contract, is true of the current code.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts:470-471: `const plain = set.paths.filter(p => !shared.has(p)); if (plain.length > 0) collect(await run(repoPath, { from: base, paths: plain, ... }))` — confirms a single net base-to-HEAD diff for plain paths, matching LLD §3.1/§9 [[c2]]'s characterization. [files: src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"`ReviewSubjectV1`/`ReviewRuntimePortsV1` and the proposed investigation/* files are genuinely new — no such symbols or module exist yet.","evidence":"Grep for ReviewSubjectV1/ReviewRuntimePortsV1/prepareReviewSubject/assertReviewSubjectFresh across src/ returns zero source-code matches (only design artifacts). Glob for src/workflow/code-review/investigation/** returns no files. The existing src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts exports an unrelated `resolveCodeReviewSubject`/`SubjectDeps`, so there is no naming collision either. [files: src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"§3.3's canonical-JSON algorithm (plain JSON records/arrays/scalars, sorted object keys, preserved array order, rejects cycles/undefined/non-finite numbers/non-plain prototypes) is labeled implicitly new work for sc1's subject-digest hashing, but an equivalent, already-hardened implementation exists and is not cited or reused.","evidence":"src/design/corpus/canonical.ts:23-84 `canonicalJson()` already does exactly this: sorts object keys (`keys.sort(compare)`), rejects cycles (`active.has(obj)` check), rejects non-finite numbers (line 48), rejects non-plain prototypes (line 54), rejects symbol/non-enumerable props. The LLD's own citations [[c1]]/[[c2]] (analyzer bundles) only surfaced `storyRangeDiff`/attribution fixtures and explicitly say the graph search was incomplete — this existing corpus module was never found or considered as a reuse seam, and the design proposes re-deriving the same canonicalization logic from scratch under src/workflow/code-review/investigation/. [files: src/design/corpus/canonical.ts, docs/epics/review-planned-changes-through-agent-investigation-E20261028c32aa605/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Have the author re-run reuse discovery against src/design/corpus/canonical.ts before building a second canonical-JSON implementation; either reuse it directly or justify in the LLD why a second, divergent canonicalization is required.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"§3.1's read-only Git object/plumbing extraction (argv-only, no replace refs/external diff/textconv/shell interpolation, object-identity verification, bounded/timeout reads) is presented as new work, but an equivalent, already-hardened read-only Git object reader with the same security properties exists and is not cited.","evidence":"src/design/corpus/sources/git-reader.ts implements exactly this: `gitEnvironment()`/`GIT_READ_ARGS` disable replace-objects, external config, hooks, attributesFile; `createGitRunner` spawns git with argv only, enforces stdout/stderr/timeout caps; `decodeObject` verifies Git's own object identity via cat-file framing + hash recomputation (lines 88-103); `treeEntry` parses tree objects for bounded path lookups. This directly overlaps the LLD's proposed `git-packets.ts`/bounded navigation, yet neither the LLD nor its cited analyze bundles mention this module as a reuse candidate. [files: src/design/corpus/sources/git-reader.ts, docs/epics/review-planned-changes-through-agent-investigation-E20261028c32aa605/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Re-check reuse of src/design/corpus/sources/git-reader.ts (createGitRunner/readPinnedSources/decodeObject/treeEntry) before authoring a second read-only Git plumbing layer with independently-maintained security hardening.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed implementation files (src/workflow/code-review/investigation/{types,subject,git-packets,source,index}.ts) do not already exist and do not collide with any existing exported symbol of the same name.","evidence":"Glob for src/workflow/code-review/investigation/** returned no files. src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts (a different, existing file) exports `resolveCodeReviewSubject`/`SubjectDeps`/`NoBuildChangesError`, none of which collide with the LLD's proposed `prepareReviewSubject`/`assertReviewSubjectFresh`. [files: src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"s1 introduces no durable/persisted data format change — sc6 is type-only, no storage writer is implemented here, and migration is additive/zero-downtime with no data rewrite, consistent with the HLD's phase-A scope (s1 only).","evidence":"HLD-c32aa60534232f36.json body.sharedContracts sc6 purpose: 'Foundational type-level ports... s4 implements durable storage'; rolloutOverview phase A 'includesStories: [s1]' with backwardCompat 'New contracts are versioned and internal... zero or ambiguous scoped packets refuse admission rather than falling back to HEAD/working-tree diff.' LLD §7 Migration states 'Zero downtime: yes — Data rewrite: no' and 'Add isolated internal sc1 preparation/navigation and sc6 type definitions, leaving production routing and persisted artifact shapes unchanged.' [files: .insrc/artifacts/HLD-c32aa60534232f36.json, docs/epics/review-planned-changes-through-agent-investigation-E20261028c32aa605/S001/LLD.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's 'owns sc1, sc6' / adjacent-scope exclusions for s2-s6 match the approved HLD's storyBoundaries exactly, so s1 does not redesign work owned by another Story or a shared contract outside its ownership.","evidence":"HLD-c32aa60534232f36.json body.storyBoundaries: s1 { owns: [sc1, sc6], depends: [] }; s2 owns sc2 depends [sc1, sc6]; s3 owns sc3; s4 owns sc4; s5 owns sc5; s6 owns sc7. The LLD §1 reproduces the same ownership and the same 'do NOT implement here' boundary text for s2-s6 verbatim (e.g. s3's 'no competing MCP phase/schema ownership; external registration belongs to s6'). [files: .insrc/artifacts/HLD-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The seven SubjectPreparationError reasons declared in §2.1 (invalid-input, unapproved-contract, stale-contract, invalid-object, ambiguous-attribution, unsupported-change, resource-limit) each map onto a distinct, detectable condition described in §5's four error cases, with no case left without a stated detection/response/typed-error triple.","evidence":"§5 'Untrusted or ambiguous changed scope' → ambiguous-attribution/invalid-object; 'Unapproved/stale/corrupt artifact or mixed Story' → unapproved-contract/stale-contract; 'Unsafe or oversized source navigation' → resource-limit (plus partial/unavailable receipts, not an error); 'Missing objects or unsupported provenance' → invalid-object/unsupported-change. All seven declared reasons are accounted for and each case states a Detection/Response/User-impact triple, consistent with the error-style conventions used elsewhere in this module family (e.g. NoBuildChangesError, DiffUnavailableError in grounding.ts/story-commits.ts). [files: docs/epics/review-planned-changes-through-agent-investigation-E20261028c32aa605/S001/LLD.md, src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of s1's four DEF acceptance criteria (ac1-ac4) is mapped to at least one named unit and one named integration test in the LLD's Acceptance mapping table.","evidence":"LLD §6 Acceptance mapping: ac1→'review-s1-ac1 unit packet parity...'+'real Git change-kind fixtures'; ac2→forged/mixed evidence rejection + concurrent foreign commit/revert fixtures; ac3→upstream basis/PLAN refusal + offline source navigation; ac4→artifact pin race + missing objects/immutable navigation. These correspond 1:1 to DEF ac1-ac4 at docs/.../DEF.md:102-105. [files: docs/epics/review-planned-changes-through-agent-investigation-E20261028c32aa605/S001/LLD.md, docs/epics/review-planned-changes-through-agent-investigation-E20261028c32aa605/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The stated test framework ('Node node:test and node:assert/strict via tsx') matches how this Story's sibling test files in the same subsystem are actually written.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/diff-attribution.test.ts:16-17 imports `{ test, after } from 'node:test'` and `assert from 'node:assert/strict'`, matching the LLD's declared framework for the new investigation/ tests. [files: src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/diff-attribution.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":2,"low":9,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-28T11:47:26.066Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
