avior with real git fixtures (e.g. 'Insrc-Story: <key>' commit messages). [files: src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/story-commits.ts, src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/diff-attribution.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ReviewSubjectV1 and ReviewRuntimePortsV1, claimed as new, do not already exist anywhere in source code.","evidence":"Grep for ReviewSubjectV1|ReviewRuntimePortsV1 across the repo returns only this Epic's own LLD/HLD artifacts and docs, no src/ hits — genuinely new types.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"canonicalJson/hashCanonical in src/design/corpus/canonical.ts exist with the signature and byte-limit semantics the LLD relies on for reuse (CORPUS_LIMITS.packageBytes = 64MiB).","evidence":"canonical.ts:5 defines CORPUS_LIMITS.packageBytes = 64*1024*1024 (64MiB) exactly as cited; canonicalJson/hashCanonical (lines 23-87) implement sorted-key canonicalization, cycle/undefined/non-finite rejection and a maxBytes ceiling capped at CORPUS_LIMITS.packageBytes, matching the design's reuse description. [files: src/design/corpus/canonical.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"createGitRunner/GIT_READ_ARGS/gitEnvironment/readPinnedSources exist and behave as the LLD describes, and decodeObject/treeEntry exist but are currently unexported, matching the plan to add 'additive named exports' rather than copy them.","evidence":"git-reader.ts defines createGitRunner (bounded stdout/stderr/timeout, no shell, GIT_READ_ARGS/gitEnvironment strip replace-objects/lazy-fetch/hooks) and readPinnedSources (regular-file blob acquisition only, no parent/mode/rename exposure) exactly as the LLD's reuse-correction claims; decodeObject and treeEntry (lines 88, 104) are declared as plain (non-exported) functions, confirming they must be newly exported, not already public. [files: src/design/corpus/sources/git-reader.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed implementation files (src/workflow/code-review/investigation/types.ts, subject.ts, git-packets.ts, source.ts, index.ts) do not yet exist, consistent with the LLD's claim that 'no call sites are claimed before s6 integration' and that these are new modules, not edits to existing ones.","evidence":"Glob for src/workflow/code-review/investigation/** returned no files, confirming the directory and its modules are genuinely new and the LLD does not misrepresent existing call sites.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design's stated byte ceiling ('no greater than existing CORPUS_LIMITS.packageBytes (64MiB)') matches the real constant, so the compatibility bound it sets for the new subject format is correctly derived from existing limits rather than invented.","evidence":"canonical.ts:5 — CORPUS_LIMITS.packageBytes = 64*1024*1024, i.e. exactly 64MiB, matching the LLD's §3.3 claim verbatim. [files: src/design/corpus/canonical.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's 'adjacent scope' table (s2-s6 ownership of sc2-sc7, with sc1/sc6 reserved to s1) matches the HLD's own story-boundary and shared-contract ownership, so s1 does not redesign work owned elsewhere.",